{"id": "EUVD-2026-65198", "enisaUuid": "cd885985-9d18-3de3-801d-d688bc3b23ec", "description": "Adminer versions 5.3.0 through 5.4.2 with the sql-log plugin enabled contain an arbitrary file write vulnerability in the ns parameter of plugins/sql-log.php. An authenticated user can supply path traversal sequences in the ns parameter to write arbitrary .sql files with attacker-controlled content to any writable directory on the host.", "datePublished": "2026-08-25T01:29:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-30T17:20:17", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vrana/adminer/security/advisories/GHSA-75xm-qwfq-9wp5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/adminer-sql-log-plugin-through-arbitrary-file-write"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-34967", "GHSA-49h4-j9cq-22wg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "42f65f8e-5765-3966-a7ce-875d7537bb40", "product": {"name": "adminer", "vendor": {"name": "vrana"}}, "product_version": "5.3.0 \u22645.4.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1739a794-c550-3c54-9be0-7cfb5d235c33", "vendor": {"name": "vrana"}}], "isExploited": false}